Effective date: July 19, 2026

Crayo respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains what information may be collected when you use the app, how it is used, and who it may be shared with.

Information We Collect
Crayo does not require account creation and does not collect any personal information such as your name, email address, or phone number.

Crayo has no analytics, advertising, or crash-reporting services built in. The app does not track you, does not build a profile of you or your child, and does not share any data with third parties for advertising or marketing purposes.

The only data the app creates is stored entirely on your device: your coloring progress, drawings, sticker collection, and settings (such as sound preferences). This information never leaves your device and is not visible to us or anyone else. Uninstalling the app deletes it.

In-App Purchases
Crayo offers a single one-time purchase ("Unlock Everything") that removes locked content. Purchases are processed entirely by Google Play Billing. Crayo never sees or stores your payment details — Google handles the transaction, and any data involved (such as your Google account and payment method) is governed by Google Play's own privacy policy: https://policies.google.com/privacy

Internet Access
The app requests internet access solely so Google Play Billing can verify and process the purchase above. Crayo makes no other network requests — there are no ads, no analytics pings, and no background data collection.

Third-Party Services
The only third-party service used by Crayo is Google Play Billing (for the optional one-time purchase). Crayo does not use Google AdMob, Firebase Analytics, Firebase Crashlytics, or any other advertising, analytics, or tracking SDK.

Children's Privacy
Crayo is designed for young children. Because the app collects no personal information, contains no ads, and includes no account creation, chat, or social features, there is no personal data collected from children of any age. A parental gate (a simple screen for grown-ups) protects the purchase and settings screens from being triggered by a child accidentally.

Data Sharing
We do not sell, rent, or share any personal information, because we do not collect any. The only data that leaves your device is the purchase request sent directly from your device to Google Play Billing when you choose to buy "Unlock Everything."

Your Choices
You can:
- use every free picture, drawing tool, and game in the app without providing any information
- delete all app data at any time by uninstalling the app, or from your device's App Info > Storage settings
- request a purchase refund through Google Play's standard refund process

Security
Since Crayo does not collect or transmit personal data, there is no personal data at risk from the app itself. Purchases are protected by Google Play's own security standards.

Changes to This Policy
This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time, for example if new features are added. Any updates will be reflected by updating the effective date above.

